;;; A real `sigilcoin` process, for the two-node tests.
;;;
;;; `test-network.sgl` runs each node as its own operating-system process so
;;; the two nodes are genuinely independent: separate VMs, separate data
;;; directories, separate SQLite handles, talking over a loopback TCP socket
;;; and nothing else. This file is what those processes run.
;;;
;;; It is the `sigilcoin` binary's own entry point and nothing more, so a
;;; test that spawns it is running the same code an operator runs:
;;;
;;; ```sh
;;; sigil -L <paths...> net-peer.sgl -- listen --regtest --data-dir DIR
;;; ```
;;;
;;; `main` takes the words after `--`, which is how the toolchain separates
;;; its own arguments from an application's, so the `-L` module paths the
;;; test passes through never reach the CLI.
;;;
;;; This is not a test file: the runner collects `test-*.sgl` and
;;; `*-test.sgl`, so it is never executed as one.

(import (sigil coin cli))

(main)
